{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtI"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma (≈ 698.045 cents). Four fifths — E→B, B→F♯, A♭→E♭, E♭→B♭ — are each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma, equal to the equal-temperament fifth","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2^(7\/12) ≈ 700.000 cents. The remaining four fifths are pure. The circle closes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly: 4×(1\/6) + 4×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}]},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Neidhardt relabeled this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specification “Small City” in his 1732 revision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardti"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE10neidhardtIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","title":"neidhardtI","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property"},"abstract":[{"text":"Neidhardt I (“Village”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724).","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/neidhardtI":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt I (“Village”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtI"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"neidhardtI","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardti","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtI","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"IvorTuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"WellTemperament","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}]}}}